<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The scores and the full information, such as the opponent bot names, are shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ C.2 Rock-Paper-Scissors Experiment Details ‣ Appendix C Additional Experimental Details ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.</p>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides a full theoretical analysis of SSoT performance on PIF. For an informal and short version, see Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We investigate the properties that the generated strings in SSoT must possess to achieve uniformity of the obtained empirical distribution, and how the deviation from a uniform distribution can be bounded for a simple sum-mod operation and standard hash functions to perform a random selection.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Settings</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we introduce the notation and definitions used throughout our analysis. Unless otherwise specified, all logarithms are base 2.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the process of selecting a sequence of <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> characters, <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}x_{2}\dots x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}x_{2}\dots x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, from an alphabet set <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted as <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also introduce an encoding function <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Enc:\Sigma\to\mathbb{Z}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Enc:\Sigma\to\mathbb{Z}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a bijection.
Since we fix a single encoding function (e.g., ASCII coding) for our analysis, we can simplify the problem by considering a sequence of length <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> with elements from <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted as <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{A}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{A}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, instead of <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we introduce our probability notation. We consider only probabilities defined on finite sets. For a random variable <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> over a finite set <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> of cardinality <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote its possible values by <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, each associated with a non-negative probability <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(x)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(x)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfying <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{x\in\mathcal{S}}P(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{x\in\mathcal{S}}P(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled from the distribution of a random variable <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now we formulate the PIF problem as follows:
The trial of sampling a random string from <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{A}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{A}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is repeated independently <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> times. Here, <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is assumed to be the same for all trials; however, this framework can accommodate variable string lengths by setting <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> to the minimum length across all <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> trials and truncating any longer strings.
Let <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be the string sampled in the <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th trial (<math id="A4.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\dots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\dots,K</annotation></semantics></math>). The empirical distribution of the hashed values in <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, obtained using hash functions <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}:\mathbb{Z}_{A}^{n}\to\mathbb{Z}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}:\mathbb{Z}_{A}^{n}\to\mathbb{Z}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, is defined as:</p>
<table id="A4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}_{\{h_{k}(s_{k})\}_{k=1}^{K}}(m)\coloneqq\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}I(h_{k}(s_{k})=m),\quad(m\in\mathbb{Z}_{M})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}_{\{h_{k}(s_{k})\}_{k=1}^{K}}(m)\coloneqq\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}I(h_{k}(s_{k})=m),\quad(m\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Note that the empirical distribution itself is a random variable, since it depends on the sampled strings <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Our goal is to make this empirical distribution as close as possible to the uniform distribution on <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, which first requires defining a distance metric between distributions. We use the following total variation distance as our metric:</p><span id="A4.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Total Variation Distance)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given two probability distributions <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and random variables <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>, both over <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the total variation distance <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{TV}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{TV}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> as:</span>
<span id="A4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{TV}}(P,Q)=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{m\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}|P(m)-Q(m)|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{TV}}(P,Q)=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{m\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}|P(m)-Q(m)|.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We also denote <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{TV}}(P,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{TV}}(P,Q)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{TV}}(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{TV}}(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We also define the following entropy measures:</p><span id="A4.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Rényi entropy)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a random variable <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and its probability distribution <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> over a set <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Rényi entropy</span> <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</span>
<span id="A4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{2}(X)=-\log\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}p(t)^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}(X)=-\log\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}p(t)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span><span id="A4.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(min-entropy)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a random variable <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and its probability distribution <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> over a set <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">min-entropy</span> <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</span>
<span id="A4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\infty}(X)=-\log\max_{t\in\mathcal{T}}p(t)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\infty}(X)=-\log\max_{t\in\mathcal{T}}p(t)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">To state our main theorems, we first need to introduce several key concepts.</p><span id="A4.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(2-universal hash functions, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Carter &amp; Wegman (1979)</a></cite>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> be finite sets.
A family of hash functions <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}=\{\,h:\mathcal{S}\to\mathcal{T}\,\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=\{\,h:\mathcal{S}\to\mathcal{T}\,\}</annotation></semantics></math> is called <span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">2-universal hash functions</span> if for any two distinct inputs <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span>
<span id="A4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr_{h\sim\mathcal{H}}[h(x_{1})=h(x_{2})]\leq\frac{1}{|\mathcal{T}|}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr_{h\sim\mathcal{H}}[h(x_{1})=h(x_{2})]\leq\frac{1}{|\mathcal{T}|},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the probability is taken over a hash function <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> chose uniformly at random from <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
</span></span>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">The above hash function is used when we leverage the Leftover Hash Lemma in Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem D.8 (TV distance bound with random hash function). ‣ D.2 Main Theorems ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.8</span></a>. The following <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-SV source is also used:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A4.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.5</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Santha-Vazirani sources, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Santha &amp; Vazirani (1986)</a></cite>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A sequence of random variables <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{1},\dots,X_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{1},\dots,X_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> taking values in <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-Santha-Vazirani source</span> if for any realization <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\sim X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\sim X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional probabilities satisfy:</span>
<span id="A4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\leq P(x_{i}|\{x_{j}\}_{0\leq j&lt;i})\leq 1-(A-1)\delta\quad\left(0\leq\delta\leq\frac{1}{A}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>A</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\leq P(x_{i}|\{x_{j}\}_{0\leq j&lt;i})\leq 1-(A-1)\delta\quad\left(0\leq\delta\leq\frac{1}{A}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hereafter, we refer to this as a <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-SV source. The Santha-Vazirani source is typically defined for binary alphabets (<math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=2</annotation></semantics></math>), but here we use a natural extension to an alphabet of size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We note that this precondition <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem5" title="Definition D.5 (Santha-Vazirani sources, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Settings ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a> allows correlations among character generation distribution at different positions; Specifically, it allows autoregressive correlation, which is unavoidable when the string is generated by an LLM.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">We also introduce several key theorems required for our proofs. First, the following theorem bounds the total variation distance between an empirical distribution and its underlying true distribution.</p><span id="A4.SS1.p10.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.6</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(An upper bound on TV distance between the empirical and the true distributions, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Weissman et al. (2003)</a></cite>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For an empirical distribution defined by Equation (<a href="#A4.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ D.1 Settings ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) calculated from a sequence of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> independent random variables <math id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> drawn from a distribution <math id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, let</span></span>
<span id="A4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)\coloneqq\frac{1}{1-2x}\ln\frac{1-x}{x},\quad\pi_{P}\coloneqq\max_{S\subseteq\mathbb{Z}_{M}}\min(P(S),1-P(S))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)\coloneqq\frac{1}{1-2x}\ln\frac{1-x}{x},\quad\pi_{P}\coloneqq\max_{S\subseteq\mathbb{Z}_{M}}\min(P(S),1-P(S)).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then,</span></span>
<span id="A4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(d_{\text{TV}}(P_{X},\hat{P}_{\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}})\geq\epsilon)\leq(2^{M}-2)e^{-K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})\epsilon^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(d_{\text{TV}}(P_{X},\hat{P}_{\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}})\geq\epsilon)\leq(2^{M}-2)e^{-K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})\epsilon^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Equivalently, for any real value <math id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the following holds with a probability of at least <math id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{TV}}(P_{X},\hat{P}_{\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}})\leq\sqrt{\frac{\ln((2^{M}-2)/\delta)}{K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{TV}}(P_{X},\hat{P}_{\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}})\leq\sqrt{\frac{\ln((2^{M}-2)/\delta)}{K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first part of this theorem, Equation (<a href="#A4.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Theorem D.6 (An upper bound on TV distance between the empirical and the true distributions, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Settings ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>), is proven in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Weissman et al., 2003</a>)</cite>. We derive Equation (<a href="#A4.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ Theorem D.6 (An upper bound on TV distance between the empirical and the true distributions, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Settings ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) as follows.
By rearranging Equation (<a href="#A4.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Theorem D.6 (An upper bound on TV distance between the empirical and the true distributions, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Settings ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>), we have:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(d_{\text{TV}}(P_{X},\hat{P}_{\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}})&lt;\epsilon)\geq 1-(2^{M}-2)e^{-K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})\epsilon^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(d_{\text{TV}}(P_{X},\hat{P}_{\{X_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}})&lt;\epsilon)\geq 1-(2^{M}-2)e^{-K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})\epsilon^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Setting <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=(2^{M}-2)e^{-K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})\epsilon^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=(2^{M}-2)e^{-K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})\epsilon^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and solving for <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> yields:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Leftrightarrow\epsilon=\sqrt{\frac{\ln((2^{M}-2)/\delta)}{K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Leftrightarrow\epsilon=\sqrt{\frac{\ln((2^{M}-2)/\delta)}{K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this into Equation (<a href="#A4.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.1 Settings ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) proves Equation (<a href="#A4.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ Theorem D.6 (An upper bound on TV distance between the empirical and the true distributions, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Settings ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, the following well-known Leftover Hash Lemma will be used (See, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vadhan (2012)</a></cite> for its proof).</p><span id="A4.SS1.p12.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.7</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Leftover Hash Lemma, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Impagliazzo et al. (1989)</a></cite>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}=\{h:\mathcal{S}\to\mathcal{T}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=\{h:\mathcal{S}\to\mathcal{T}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a 2-universal hash family, and let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be a random variable for a hash function chosen uniformly at random from <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any random variable <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, the total variation distance between the joint distribution of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H,h_{H}(X))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H,h_{H}(X))</annotation></semantics></math> and the ideal distribution <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H,U_{\mathcal{T}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H,U_{\mathcal{T}})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the uniform distribution on <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, is bounded as follows:</span></span>
<span id="A4.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{TV}((H,h_{H}(X)),(H,U_{\mathcal{T}}))\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{|\mathcal{T}|2^{-H_{2}(X)}}\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{|\mathcal{T}|2^{-H_{\infty}(X)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{TV}((H,h_{H}(X)),(H,U_{\mathcal{T}}))\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{|\mathcal{T}|2^{-H_{2}(X)}}\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{|\mathcal{T}|2^{-H_{\infty}(X)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Main Theorems</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our goal is to prove the following two theorems.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.8</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(TV distance bound with random hash function)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{n}=\{X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{n}=\{X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of random variables over <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> that constitutes a <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-SV source. Using a 2-universal hash family <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}=\{h:\mathbb{Z}_{A}^{n}\to\mathbb{Z}_{M}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=\{h:\mathbb{Z}_{A}^{n}\to\mathbb{Z}_{M}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the total variation distance is bounded by:</span></span>
<span id="A4.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{TV}}((H,h_{H}(X^{n})),(H,U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}}))\leq\frac{\sqrt{M}}{2}2^{-\frac{n}{2}\log\frac{1}{(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}}}=2^{\log\frac{\sqrt{M}}{2}-n\frac{A-1}{\log_{e}2}\delta+\mathcal{O}(n\delta^{2})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>M</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mi>M</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{TV}}((H,h_{H}(X^{n})),(H,U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}}))\leq\frac{\sqrt{M}}{2}2^{-\frac{n}{2}\log\frac{1}{(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}}}=2^{\log\frac{\sqrt{M}}{2}-n\frac{A-1}{\log_{e}2}\delta+\mathcal{O}(n\delta^{2})},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the uniform distribution on <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. This equation shows that for a given <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-SV source, the total variation distance can be made arbitrarily small by choosing a sufficiently large <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, for small <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="δ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">δ</annotation></semantics></math>, the distance becomes negligible if the string length n satisfies:</span></span>
<span id="A4.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\gg\frac{\log_{e}\frac{\sqrt{M}}{2}}{(A-1)\delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≫</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mi>M</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\gg\frac{\log_{e}\frac{\sqrt{M}}{2}}{(A-1)\delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Furthermore, for the total variation distance between the empirical distribution and the uniform distribution, the following holds with a probability of at least <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta^{\prime}-\delta^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta^{\prime}-\delta^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime},\delta^{\prime\prime}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime},\delta^{\prime\prime}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A4.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{TV}}(\hat{P}_{\{h((x^{n})_{k})\}_{k=1}^{K}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{\sqrt{M}}{2\delta^{\prime\prime}}2^{-\frac{n}{2}\log\frac{1}{(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}}}+\sqrt{\frac{\ln((2^{M}-2)/\delta^{\prime})}{K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>M</mi></msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{TV}}(\hat{P}_{\{h((x^{n})_{k})\}_{k=1}^{K}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{\sqrt{M}}{2\delta^{\prime\prime}}2^{-\frac{n}{2}\log\frac{1}{(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}}}+\sqrt{\frac{\ln((2^{M}-2)/\delta^{\prime})}{K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This theorem guarantees the uniformness of the empirical distribution given that the string length is long enough. As for the choice of the hash function, the diversity among different responses is <span id="A4.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">not</span> required. 2-universal hash functions can be realized as a random linear map on a finite field <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq M</annotation></semantics></math> and then taking modulo <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Carter &amp; Wegman, 1979</a>)</cite>, which is within the capabilities of LLMs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.9</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(TV distance bound with sum-and-mod strategy)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of random variables over <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, and that these are independent with the probability distribution <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>).
We embed each element <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and compute their sum modulo <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A4.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}=\sum_{1\leq i\leq n}x_{i}\mod M." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>mod</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}=\sum_{1\leq i\leq n}x_{i}\mod M.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the random variable corresponding to <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability distribution <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{S_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{S_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let the Fourier transform of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be:</span></span>
<span id="A4.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\eta}_{i}(k)=\sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}e^{2\pi ikx/M}\eta_{i}(x),\quad k\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\eta}_{i}(k)=\sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}e^{2\pi ikx/M}\eta_{i}(x),\quad k\in\mathbb{Z}_{M},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where, for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we embed the probability distribution over <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> to the one over <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> with modulo (if <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&lt;A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&lt;A</annotation></semantics></math>) or <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> padding (if <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&gt;A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&gt;A</annotation></semantics></math>) operations.
Then, the total variation distance is bounded as follows:</span></span>
<span id="A4.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{TV}}(P_{S_{n}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{d|M,\,d&gt;1}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}t=1\\
\gcd(t,d)=1\end{subarray}}^{d-1}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left|\widehat{\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})}(t)\right|^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>gcd</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{TV}}(P_{S_{n}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{d|M,\,d&gt;1}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}t=1\\
\gcd(t,d)=1\end{subarray}}^{d-1}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left|\widehat{\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})}(t)\right|^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{d}:\mathbb{Z}_{M}\to\mathbb{Z}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{d}:\mathbb{Z}_{M}\to\mathbb{Z}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the projection mapping an element to its value modulo <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m20" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is the pushforward of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as:</span></span>
<span id="A4.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})(r)\coloneqq\sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}_{M},x\equiv r\,(\text{mod}\,d)}\eta_{i}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">mod</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})(r)\coloneqq\sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}_{M},x\equiv r\,(\text{mod}\,d)}\eta_{i}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the Fourier transform over the group <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Furthermore, using total variation distance, the following bounds hold:</span></span>
<span id="A4.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{TV}}(P_{S_{n}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{d|M,\,d&gt;1}\varphi(d)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left(2d_{\text{TV}}(\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i}),U_{\mathbb{Z}_{d}})\right)^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{TV}}(P_{S_{n}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{d|M,\,d&gt;1}\varphi(d)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left(2d_{\text{TV}}(\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i}),U_{\mathbb{Z}_{d}})\right)^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(d)</annotation></semantics></math> is Euler’s totient function.
Moreover, for an empirical distribution derived from <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> independent samples <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{n}^{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{n}^{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following holds with a probability of at least <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="A4.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{TV}}(\hat{P}_{\{s_{n}^{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{d|M,\,d&gt;1}\varphi(d)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left(2d_{\text{TV}}(\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i}),U_{\mathbb{Z}_{d}})\right)^{2}}+\sqrt{\frac{\ln((2^{M}-2)/\delta^{\prime})}{K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TV</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{TV}}(\hat{P}_{\{s_{n}^{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{d|M,\,d&gt;1}\varphi(d)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left(2d_{\text{TV}}(\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i}),U_{\mathbb{Z}_{d}})\right)^{2}}+\sqrt{\frac{\ln((2^{M}-2)/\delta^{\prime})}{K\phi(\pi_{P_{X}})}},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This theorem focuses on a simple sum-mod operation, which is in fact employed by LLMs (see CoT analysis in Section <a href="#S5.SS3.SSS1" title="5.3.1 CoT Strategy Analysis ‣ 5.3 Analysis ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3.1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Proof of theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem D.8 (TV distance bound with random hash function). ‣ D.2 Main Theorems ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.8</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we prove the following lemma.</span></p><span id="A4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.10</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Rényi entropy of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-SV-sources)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a random variable <math id="A4.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(X_{1},\dots,X_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(X_{1},\dots,X_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to a sequence of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A4.Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-SV sources, its Rényi entropy <math id="A4.Thmtheorem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by:</span></span>
<span id="A4.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-n\log\left[(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}\right]\leq H_{2}(X)\leq n\log A" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-n\log\left[(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}\right]\leq H_{2}(X)\leq n\log A</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The collision probability of <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{x_{1},\dots,x_{n}}P(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{x_{1},\dots,x_{n}}P(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1}}P(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})^{2}\sum_{x_{n}}P(x_{n}|\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1}}P(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})^{2}\sum_{x_{n}}P(x_{n}|\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1}}P(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})^{2}\sum_{x_{n}}(P(x_{n}|\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1}}P(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})^{2}\sum_{x_{n}}(P(x_{n}|\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqqcolon\sum_{x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1}}P(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})^{2}D(\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqqcolon\sum_{x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1}}P(x_{1},\dots,x_{n-1})^{2}D(\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we bound the term <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})\geq\frac{1}{A}\left(\sum_{x_{n}}P(x_{n}|\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})\right)^{2}=\frac{1}{A}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>A</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></munder><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>A</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})\geq\frac{1}{A}\left(\sum_{x_{n}}P(x_{n}|\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})\right)^{2}=\frac{1}{A}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">We define <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})\coloneqq P(x_{n}|\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})\coloneqq P(x_{n}|\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, and noting that <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D(\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D(\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{n}}(\delta+E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{n}}(\delta+E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=A\delta^{2}+2\delta\sum_{x_{n}}E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})+\sum_{x_{n}}(E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=A\delta^{2}+2\delta\sum_{x_{n}}E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})+\sum_{x_{n}}(E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\delta-A\delta^{2}+\sum_{x_{n}}(E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\delta-A\delta^{2}+\sum_{x_{n}}(E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Here,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\sum_{x_{n}}E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\sum_{x_{n}}E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{n}}E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})^{2}+\sum_{x_{n},x_{n}^{\prime}(x_{n}\neq x_{n}^{\prime})}E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})E(x_{n}^{\prime},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x_{n}}E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})^{2}+\sum_{x_{n},x_{n}^{\prime}(x_{n}\neq x_{n}^{\prime})}E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})E(x_{n}^{\prime},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{x_{n}}E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})^{2}\quad(\because E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})\geq 0)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></munder></mstyle><mi>E</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∵</mo><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{x_{n}}E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})^{2}\quad(\because E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})\geq 0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Combining it with <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sum_{x_{n}}E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}=(1-A\delta)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sum_{x_{n}}E(x_{n},\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n}))^{2}=(1-A\delta)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, Equation (<a href="#A4.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Proof. ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Proof of theorem ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) becomes:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D(\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D(\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\delta-A\delta^{2}+(1-A\delta)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\delta-A\delta^{2}+(1-A\delta)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-2(A-1)\delta-A\delta^{2}+A^{2}\delta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-2(A-1)\delta-A\delta^{2}+A^{2}\delta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+A^{2}\delta^{2}-A\delta^{2}-(A-1)^{2}\delta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+A^{2}\delta^{2}-A\delta^{2}-(A-1)^{2}\delta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{A}\leq D(\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})\leq(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>A</mi></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{A}\leq D(\{x_{j}\}_{j&lt;n})\leq(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Applying this result inductively to Equation (<a href="#A4.E25" title="Equation 25 ‣ Proof. ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Proof of theorem ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>), we get:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{A^{n}}\leq\sum_{x_{1},\dots,x_{n}}P(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})^{2}\leq[(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}]^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{A^{n}}\leq\sum_{x_{1},\dots,x_{n}}P(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})^{2}\leq[(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}]^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">By the monotonicity of the logarithm, we obtain the final bound on the Rényi entropy:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-n\log\left[(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}\right]\leq H_{2}(X)\leq n\log A." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-n\log\left[(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}\right]\leq H_{2}(X)\leq n\log A.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem10" title="Lemma D.10 (Rényi entropy of 𝛿-SV-sources). ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Proof of theorem ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.10</span></a> with the Leftover Hash Lemma (Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma D.7 (Leftover Hash Lemma, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Settings ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.7</span></a>), we can bound the distance as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{TV}((H,h_{H}(X)),(H,U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}}))\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{M2^{-H_{2}(X)}}\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{M2^{-n\log\frac{1}{(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{TV}((H,h_{H}(X)),(H,U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}}))\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{M2^{-H_{2}(X)}}\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{M2^{-n\log\frac{1}{(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">This establishes Equation (<a href="#A4.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Theorem D.8 (TV distance bound with random hash function). ‣ D.2 Main Theorems ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).
From Markov’s inequality, for any <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta^{\prime\prime}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta^{\prime\prime}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{TV}(P_{h_{H}(X)},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{1}{2\delta^{\prime\prime}}\sqrt{M2^{-n\log\frac{1}{(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{TV}(P_{h_{H}(X)},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{1}{2\delta^{\prime\prime}}\sqrt{M2^{-n\log\frac{1}{(1-(A-1)\delta)^{2}+(A-1)\delta^{2}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, by applying the triangle inequality and union bound along with Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem D.6 (An upper bound on TV distance between the empirical and the true distributions, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Settings ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.6</span></a>, we establish Equation (<a href="#A4.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Theorem D.8 (TV distance bound with random hash function). ‣ D.2 Main Theorems ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), which completes the proof of Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem D.8 (TV distance bound with random hash function). ‣ D.2 Main Theorems ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.8</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem D.9 (TV distance bound with sum-and-mod strategy). ‣ D.2 Main Theorems ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.9</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We consider the sum <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}x_{i}\mod M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>mod</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}x_{i}\mod M</annotation></semantics></math>.
The Fourier transform of <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{S_{n}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{S_{n}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{P_{S_{n}}}(k)=\sum_{s\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}e^{2\pi iks/M}P_{S_{n}}(s)=\sum_{s\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}e^{2\pi iks/M}\sum_{\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n},\sum_{i}x_{i}=s}P(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\widehat{\eta_{i}}(k)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{P_{S_{n}}}(k)=\sum_{s\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}e^{2\pi iks/M}P_{S_{n}}(s)=\sum_{s\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}e^{2\pi iks/M}\sum_{\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n},\sum_{i}x_{i}=s}P(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\widehat{\eta_{i}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Plancherel’s theorem for Fourier transforms on finite groups <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Diaconis &amp; Shahshahani, 1981</a>)</cite>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{s\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}P_{S_{n}}(s)^{2}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}|\widehat{P_{S_{n}}}(k)|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{s\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}P_{S_{n}}(s)^{2}=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}|\widehat{P_{S_{n}}}(k)|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\text{TV}}(P_{S_{n}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\text{TV}}(P_{S_{n}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\sqrt{M}}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{s\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}\left(P_{S_{n}}(s)-\frac{1}{M}\right)^{2}}\quad(\because\text{Cauchy-Schwarz inequality})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>M</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∵</mo><mtext>Cauchy-Schwarz inequality</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\sqrt{M}}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{s\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}\left(P_{S_{n}}(s)-\frac{1}{M}\right)^{2}}\quad(\because\text{Cauchy-Schwarz inequality})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{M}}{2}\sqrt{\frac{1}{M}\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}|\widehat{P_{S_{n}}}(k)|^{2}-\frac{1}{M}}\quad(\because\eqref{eq:palancherel})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>M</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∵</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#A4.E35" title="Equation 35 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{M}}{2}\sqrt{\frac{1}{M}\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}|\widehat{P_{S_{n}}}(k)|^{2}-\frac{1}{M}}\quad(\because\eqref{eq:palancherel})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}_{M},k&gt;0}|\widehat{P_{S_{n}}}(k)|^{2}}\quad\left(\because|\widehat{P_{S_{n}}}(0)|=1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∵</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}_{M},k&gt;0}|\widehat{P_{S_{n}}}(k)|^{2}}\quad\left(\because|\widehat{P_{S_{n}}}(0)|=1\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{k=1}^{M-1}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left|\widehat{\eta_{i}}(k)\right|^{2}}\quad(\because\eqref{eq:total_p_fourier})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∵</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#A4.E34" title="Equation 34 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{k=1}^{M-1}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left|\widehat{\eta_{i}}(k)\right|^{2}}\quad(\because\eqref{eq:total_p_fourier}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we decompose <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\eta_{i}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\eta_{i}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(k)\coloneqq M/\gcd(M,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>gcd</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(k)\coloneqq M/\gcd(M,k)</annotation></semantics></math>、<math id="A4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(k)\coloneqq k/\gcd(M,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>gcd</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(k)\coloneqq k/\gcd(M,k)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{2\pi ixk/M}=e^{2\pi ixt(k)/d(k)}=e^{2\pi i\pi_{d}(x)t(k)/d(k)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{2\pi ixk/M}=e^{2\pi ixt(k)/d(k)}=e^{2\pi i\pi_{d}(x)t(k)/d(k)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{d}(x)=x\mod d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{d}(x)=x\mod d</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\eta_{i}}(k)=\sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}e^{2\pi i\pi_{d}(x)t(k)/d(k)}\eta(x)=\sum_{r=0}^{d(k)-1}e^{2\pi irt(k)/d(k)}\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})(r)\eqqcolon\widehat{\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})}(t(k))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≕</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\eta_{i}}(k)=\sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}_{M}}e^{2\pi i\pi_{d}(x)t(k)/d(k)}\eta(x)=\sum_{r=0}^{d(k)-1}e^{2\pi irt(k)/d(k)}\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})(r)\eqqcolon\widehat{\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})}(t(k)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A4.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})(r)\coloneqq\sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}_{M},x\equiv r\,(\text{mod }d)}\eta_{i}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>mod </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})(r)\coloneqq\sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}_{M},x\equiv r\,(\text{mod }d)}\eta_{i}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting Equation (<a href="#A4.E38" title="Equation 38 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>) into Equation (<a href="#A4.E36" title="Equation 36 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>) and grouping terms by common divisors of <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{TV}}(P_{S_{n}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}d&gt;1\\
d|M\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}t=1\\
\gcd(t,d)=1\end{subarray}}^{d-1}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left|\widehat{\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})}(t)\right|^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>gcd</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{TV}}(P_{S_{n}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}d&gt;1\\
d|M\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}t=1\\
\gcd(t,d)=1\end{subarray}}^{d-1}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left|\widehat{\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})}(t)\right|^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}(d)\coloneqq\max_{1\leq t\leq d-1,\,\gcd(t,d)=1}|\widehat{\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})}(t)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>gcd</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}(d)\coloneqq\max_{1\leq t\leq d-1,\,\gcd(t,d)=1}|\widehat{\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})}(t)|</annotation></semantics></math>. The bound becomes:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\text{TV}}(P_{S_{n}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\text{TV}}(P_{S_{n}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}d&gt;1\\
d|M\end{subarray}}\varphi(d)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left|\alpha_{i}(d)\right|^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}d&gt;1\\
d|M\end{subarray}}\varphi(d)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left|\alpha_{i}(d)\right|^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is Euler’s totient function.
Here, noting that</span></p>
<table id="A4.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\widehat{\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})}(t)|=|\sum_{r}e^{2\pi ir/d}\left(\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})(r)-\frac{1}{d}\right)|\leq\sum_{r}\left|\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})(r)-\frac{1}{d}\right|=2d_{\text{TV}}(\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i}),U_{\mathbb{Z}_{d}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>r</mi></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>r</mi></munder><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})}(t)|=|\sum_{r}e^{2\pi ir/d}\left(\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})(r)-\frac{1}{d}\right)|\leq\sum_{r}\left|\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i})(r)-\frac{1}{d}\right|=2d_{\text{TV}}(\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i}),U_{\mathbb{Z}_{d}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha_{i}(d)\leq 2d_{\text{TV}}(\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i}),U_{\mathbb{Z}_{d}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}(d)\leq 2d_{\text{TV}}(\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i}),U_{\mathbb{Z}_{d}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.SS4.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text"> also holds. Therefore, Equation (<a href="#A4.E41" title="Equation 41 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) becomes:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{TV}}(P_{S_{n}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}d&gt;1\\
d|M\end{subarray}}\varphi(d)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left|2d_{\text{TV}}(\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i}),U_{\mathbb{Z}_{d}})\right|^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{TV}}(P_{S_{n}},U_{\mathbb{Z}_{M}})\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}d&gt;1\\
d|M\end{subarray}}\varphi(d)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left|2d_{\text{TV}}(\pi_{d*}(\eta_{i}),U_{\mathbb{Z}_{d}})\right|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, applying the triangle inequality along with Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem D.6 (An upper bound on TV distance between the empirical and the true distributions, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Settings ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.6</span></a> establishes Equation (<a href="#A4.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ Theorem D.9 (TV distance bound with sum-and-mod strategy). ‣ D.2 Main Theorems ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), completing the proof of Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem D.9 (TV distance bound with sum-and-mod strategy). ‣ D.2 Main Theorems ‣ Appendix D Full Theoretical Analysis of SSoT Performance on PIF ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.9</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Biased Target Distribution</h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we show that we can apply our analysis to the biased target distribution, for a given biased distribution <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(i)=p_{i}\,(i=1,\dots,M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(i)=p_{i}\,(i=1,\dots,M)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a given target distribution <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, choose a sufficiently large integer <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{u_{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{u_{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the uniform distribution on <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choose integers <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\in\{0,\ldots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\in\{0,\ldots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{M}a_{i}=N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{M}a_{i}=N</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\approx Np_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\approx Np_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then we partition <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> into sets <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A_{i}|=a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{i}|=a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{Z}_{N}\to\mathbb{Z}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{Z}_{N}\to\mathbb{Z}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(z)=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(z)=i</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then the pushforward of the uniform distribution over <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{(N)}:=f_{*}P_{u_{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{(N)}:=f_{*}P_{u_{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>, approximates <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, since total variation is contractive under pushforward:
<math id="A4.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{TV}}(f_{*}P,\,f_{*}Q)\leq d_{\mathrm{TV}}(P,\,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{TV}}(f_{*}P,\,f_{*}Q)\leq d_{\mathrm{TV}}(P,\,Q)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This follows from the alternative and equivalent definition of total variation distance, <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{TV}}(P,Q)=\max_{A\subset\mathbb{Z}_{N}}|P(A)-Q(A)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>TV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{TV}}(P,Q)=\max_{A\subset\mathbb{Z}_{N}}|P(A)-Q(A)|</annotation></semantics></math>, as the maximization over subsets of <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a smaller collection of events than the maximization over all subsets of <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Hence any bound proved for the uniform base <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{u_{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{u_{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> carries over to <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, up to the rounding error
<math id="A4.SS5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{TV}}(P^{(N)},P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{TV}}(P^{(N)},P)</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be made arbitrarily small by increasing <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus it suffices to analyze the uniform distribution on <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>LLM Outputs for SSoT prompting</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we list example outputs of deepseek-r1 in our experiments. Since the full reasoning trace tends to be long, we show the full final outputs and only the important fraction of the full reasoning trace.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Probabilistic Instruction Following</h3>

<section id="A5.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.1.1 </span>Sum-Mod Strategy in Unbiased PIF</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As for unbiased PIF, deepseek-r1 tends to employ a simple sum-mod strategy as we elaborated in Section <a href="#S5.SS3.SSS1" title="5.3.1 CoT Strategy Analysis ‣ 5.3 Analysis ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3.1</span></a>. Here we show the output for the 2-choice task in Section <a href="#S5.SS1.SSS1" title="5.1.1 Performance Across Multiple LLMs ‣ 5.1 Probabilistic Instruction Following ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1.1</span></a> (coin flip).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Output:</p><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;random_string&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">7fG2#kL9!pY4@zR6%vD1*sN0&amp;qX5$wT8</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;/random_string&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;thinking&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.5.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We need to choose between "heads" and "tails" with equal probability (0.5 each). The random seed string "7fG2#kL9!pY4@zR6%vD1*sN0&amp;qX5$wT8" must be used to determine the outcome. To ensure fairness and use the entire string, we compute the sum of the ASCII values of all characters in the string. The parity of this sum (mod 2) will decide the result:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.6.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">- Sum mod 2 = 0 → "heads"</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.7.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">- Sum mod 2 = 1 → "tails"</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.8.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.9.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The string has 32 characters. After evaluating each character:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.10.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">- Characters with odd ASCII values: ’7’ (55), ’G’ (71), ’#’ (35), ’k’ (107), ’9’ (57), ’!’ (33), ’Y’ (89), ’%’ (37), ’1’ (49), ’s’ (115), ’q’ (113), ’5’ (53), ’w’ (119) → 13 characters.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.11.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">- Characters with even ASCII values: 19 characters.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.12.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">The number of characters with odd ASCII values is 13. Since 13 mod 2 = 1, the sum mod 2 is 1.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.13.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the result is "tails".</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.14.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;/thinking&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.15.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;answer&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.16.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">tails</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.1.17.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.p1.p17.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;/answer&gt;</span>
</span></span></span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Reasoning (The sum-mod calculation part):</p><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">...</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">  We generated: "7fG2#kL9!pY4@zR6%vD1*sN0&amp;qX5$wT8"</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">  Let’s compute the sum mod 2 quickly:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.5.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">...</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.6.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">  Let’s go character by character and determine if ord(c) is odd or even.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.7.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.8.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">  ’7’: 55 -&gt; odd</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.9.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">  ’f’: 102 -&gt; even</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.10.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">  ’G’: 71 -&gt; odd</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.11.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">...</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.12.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">  ’w’: 119 -&gt; odd</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.13.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">  ’T’: 84 -&gt; even</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.14.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">  ’8’: 56 -&gt; even</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.15.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.16.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">  Now count the odd ones:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.17.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.18.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p18.1" class="ltx_p">      7: odd -&gt; count=1</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.19.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p19.1" class="ltx_p">      f: even -&gt; 1</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.20.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p20.1" class="ltx_p">      G: odd -&gt; 2</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.21" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.21.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p21.1" class="ltx_p">  ...</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.22" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.22.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p22.1" class="ltx_p">      w: odd -&gt; 13</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.23" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.23.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p23.1" class="ltx_p">      T: even -&gt; 13</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.24" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.24.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p24.1" class="ltx_p">      8: even -&gt; 13</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.25" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.25.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.26" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.26.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p26.1" class="ltx_p">  So there are 13 odd characters.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.27" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.27.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.28" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.28.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p28" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p28.1" class="ltx_p">  13 mod 2 = 1, so sum mod 2 = 1 -&gt; tails.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.29" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.29.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.30" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.30.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p30" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p30.1" class="ltx_p">  So we choose "tails".</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.31" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.1.31.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p31" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.p1.p31.1" class="ltx_p">...</span>
</span></span></span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.1.2 </span>Rolling Hash in Biased PIF</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also show the rolling hash CoT, which is used more frequently in the biased PIF setting. Here we show the output for the biased 2-choice task in Section <a href="#S5.SS1.SSS1" title="5.1.1 Performance Across Multiple LLMs ‣ 5.1 Probabilistic Instruction Following ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1.1</span></a> (coin flip).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Output:</p><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;random_string&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">8sD$kF3!pL9@zG2#rH4%tJ6&amp;uK0*oM1</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;/random_string&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;thinking&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.5.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We are to choose between "heads" and "tails" with probabilities 0.3 and 0.7 respectively. The random string "8sD$kF3!pL9@zG2#rH4%tJ6&amp;uK0*oM1" will be used to derive a deterministic value for this decision.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.6.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.7.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">To convert the string into a number between 0 and 99 (inclusive):</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.8.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">1. Process each character in the string sequentially.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.9.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">2. Convert each character to its ASCII value.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.10.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">3. Use the formula: \( \text{num} = (\text{num} \times 256 + \text{ASCII value}) \mod 100 \) for each character, starting with num = 0.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.11.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.12.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Step-by-step computation:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.13.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">- Start: num = 0</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.14.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">- ’8’ (56): num = (0 × 256 + 56) % 100 = 56</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.15.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">- ’s’ (115): num = (56 × 256 + 115) % 100 = (14336 + 115) % 100 = 14451 % 100 = 51</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.16.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">- ’D’ (68): num = (51 × 256 + 68) % 100 = (13056 + 68) % 100 = 13124 % 100 = 24</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.17.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p17.1" class="ltx_p">...</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.18.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p18.1" class="ltx_p">- ’o’ (111): num = (42 × 256 + 111) % 100 = (10752 + 111) % 100 = 10863 % 100 = 63</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.19.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p19.1" class="ltx_p">- ’M’ (77): num = (63 × 256 + 77) % 100 = (16128 + 77) % 100 = 16205 % 100 = 5</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.20.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p20.1" class="ltx_p">- ’1’ (49): num = (5 × 256 + 49) % 100 = (1280 + 49) % 100 = 1329 % 100 = 29</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.21" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.21.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.22" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.22.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p22.1" class="ltx_p">Final derived value: 29 (out of 0–99 range).</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.23" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.23.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.24" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.24.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p24.1" class="ltx_p">Decision rule:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.25" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.25.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p25" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p25.1" class="ltx_p">- If the value &lt; 30 (30% probability), choose "heads".</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.26" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.26.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p26.1" class="ltx_p">- Otherwise, choose "tails" (70% probability).</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.27" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.27.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.28" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.28.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p28" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p28.1" class="ltx_p">Since 29 &lt; 30, we select "heads".</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.29" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.29.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p29" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p29.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;/thinking&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.30" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.30.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p30" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p30.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;answer&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.31" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.31.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p31" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p31.1" class="ltx_p">heads</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.32" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.1.32.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p32" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p2.p1.p32.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;/answer&gt;</span>
</span></span></span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Reasoning (The rolling-hash calculation part):</p><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">...</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.2.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">        Alternatively, we can compute the entire sum mod 100 without building the huge number by processing each digit:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">          num = 0</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.5.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">          for i in range(len(s)):</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.6.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">              num = (num * 256 + ord(s[i])) % 100</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.7.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">...</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.8.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">   We generate the random string: "8sD$kF3!pL9@zG2#rH4%tJ6&amp;uK0*oM1"</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.9.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.10.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">   Then we compute n:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.11.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.12.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">        s = "8sD$kF3!pL9@zG2#rH4%tJ6&amp;uK0*oM1"</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.13.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.14.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">        We do:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.15.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.16.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">          ’8’ -&gt; 56: num=56</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.17.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p17.1" class="ltx_p">          ’s’ -&gt; 115: num = (56*256+115) % 100 = (14336+115) % 100 = 14451 % 100 = 51</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.18.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p18.1" class="ltx_p">          ’D’ -&gt; 68: num = (51*256+68) % 100 = (13056+68) % 100 = 13124 % 100 = 24</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.19.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p19.1" class="ltx_p">...</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.20.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p20.1" class="ltx_p">          ’o’ -&gt; 111: num = (42*256+111) % 100 = (10752+111) % 100 = 10863 % 100 = 63</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.21" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.21.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p21.1" class="ltx_p">          ’M’ -&gt; 77: num = (63*256+77) % 100 = (16128+77) % 100 = 16205 % 100 = 5</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.22" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.22.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.22.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p22.1" class="ltx_p">          ’1’ -&gt; 49: num = (5*256+49) % 100 = (1280+49) % 100 = 1329 % 100 = 29</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.23" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.23.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.24" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.24.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p24.1" class="ltx_p">        n = 29.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.25" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.25.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.26" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.26.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p26.1" class="ltx_p">        Since 29 &lt; 30, we choose "heads".</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.27" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.27.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.28" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.28.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p28" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p28.1" class="ltx_p">   Therefore, we’ll output "heads".</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.29" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.1.29.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p29" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS1.SSS2.p3.p1.p29.1" class="ltx_p">...</span>
</span></span></span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Diversity-Aware Generation in NoveltyBench</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In DAG tasks, LLM tends to use the templating and local random selection approach as we demonstrated in Section <a href="#S5.SS3.SSS1" title="5.3.1 CoT Strategy Analysis ‣ 5.3 Analysis ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3.1</span></a>. Here we show an example output for a creative question, “Write a short fable about a lemur and a light bulb.”</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Output:</p><span id="A5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;random_string&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Rw6#jK9!pL@3z$mQ*4xY7&amp;fN1</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;/random_string&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;thinking&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.5.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This fable requires creativity and randomness. The seed string "Rw6#jK9!pL@3z$mQ*4xY7&amp;fN1" will guide all story decisions. Steps:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.6.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.7.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">1. **Seed Application**: Convert the string into numerical values using ASCII codes, then use modular arithmetic to determine key elements:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.8.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">   - First 5 chars (R,w,6,#,j) → Sum ASCII = 82+119+54+35+106 = 396 → Mod 3 = 0 (setting: urban alley)</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.9.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">   - Next 5 (K,9,!,p,L) → Sum = 75+57+33+112+76 = 353 → Mod 4 = 1 (lemur trait: philosophical)</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.10.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">   - Next 5 (@,3,z,$,m) → Sum = 64+51+122+36+109 = 382 → Mod 2 = 0 (bulb state: flickering)</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.11.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">   - Next 5 (Q,*,4,x,Y) → Sum = 81+42+52+120+89 = 384 → Mod 3 = 0 (conflict: misinterpretation)</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.12.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">   - Last 6 (7,&amp;,f,N,1) → Sum = 55+38+102+78+49 = 322 → Mod 2 = 0 (moral: perception vs reality)</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.13.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.14.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">2. **Plot Outline**:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.15.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">   - Setting: Urban alley (0) → Gritty city environment</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.16.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">   - Lemur: Named Zephyr (from seed letters "jK9"), philosophical (1) → Ponders existence</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.17.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p17.1" class="ltx_p">   - Bulb: Flickering (0) → Unpredictable light source</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.18.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p18.1" class="ltx_p">   - Conflict: Misinterpretation (0) → Lemur believes bulb is a dying star</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.19.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p19.1" class="ltx_p">   - Moral: Perception ≠ reality (0) → Truth requires deeper understanding</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.20.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.21" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.21.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p21.1" class="ltx_p">3. **Narrative Flow**:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.22" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.22.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p22.1" class="ltx_p">   - Start with Zephyr’s urban life</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.23" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.23.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p23.1" class="ltx_p">   - Discovery of flickering bulb</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.24" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.24.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p24.1" class="ltx_p">   - Philosophical monologue about stars</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.25" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.25.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p25" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p25.1" class="ltx_p">   - Climax: Human fixes bulb, shattering illusion</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.26" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.26.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p26.1" class="ltx_p">   - Moral revelation</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.27" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.27.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.28" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.28.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.28.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p28" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p28.1" class="ltx_p">4. **Seed Utilization**: All 20 characters directly influenced character, setting, conflict, and theme. No element is arbitrary.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.29" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.29.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p29" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p29.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;/thinking&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.30" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.30.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p30" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p30.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;answer&gt;</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.31" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.31.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.31.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p31" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p31.1" class="ltx_p">In a rain-slicked alley of a bustling city, Zephyr the lemur perched atop a dumpster, his reflective nature often leading him to ponder life’s mysteries. One twilight, he spotted a flickering light bulb dangling from a frayed wire<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p31.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\CJK@punctchar</span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p31.1.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\CJK@uniPunct</span>0"80"94its glow sputtering like a trapped firefly.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.32" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.32.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.33" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.33.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.33.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.33.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.33.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p33" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p33.1" class="ltx_p">"Ah, a fallen star!" Zephyr murmured, his eyes wide with reverence. "How tragic, to burn alone in this concrete wilderness." Each night, he<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p33.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\CJK@punctchar</span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p33.1.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\CJK@uniPunct</span>0"80"99d visit the bulb, whispering consolations: "Your light may wane, dear star, but your essence is eternal."</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.34" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.34.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.35" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.35.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.35.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.35.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.35.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p35" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p35.1" class="ltx_p">One evening, a human trudged into the alley. Zephyr watched, breath bated, as the giant fiddled with the wire. With a *click*, the bulb flared steady and bright. The human grumbled, "Stupid loose socket," and left.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.36" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.36.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.37" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.37.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.37.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.37.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.37.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p37" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p37.1" class="ltx_p">Zephyr<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p37.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\CJK@punctchar</span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p37.1.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\CJK@uniPunct</span>0"80"99s heart sank. The "star" was merely glass and tungsten<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p37.1.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\CJK@punctchar</span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p37.1.4" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\CJK@uniPunct</span>0"80"94a humble human tool. Yet in its new, unwavering light, he saw a deeper truth: Wisdom isn<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p37.1.5" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\CJK@punctchar</span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p37.1.6" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\CJK@uniPunct</span>0"80"99t in clinging to pretty illusions, but in seeking the socket that anchors reality.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.38" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.38.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.39" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.39.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.39.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.39.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.39.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p39" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p39.1" class="ltx_p">Moral: What glimmers is not always gold; true understanding demands we trace the wire back to its source.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.40" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.1.40.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p40" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.p1.p40.1" class="ltx_p">&lt;/answer&gt;</span>
</span></span></span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In its reasoning trace, LLM tried to create several example stories with different random string seeds and decided how to perform the generation in its output. LLM also creates a draft for the output, but the sampling and story construction were often done in the final output step.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Reasoning (story construction breakdown part):</p><span id="A5.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">...</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"> Now, for the thinking step:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">   We’ll use the random string to make decisions about:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">     - The setting (e.g., forest, city, etc.)</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.5.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">     - The lemur’s personality and motivation</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.6.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">     - The light bulb’s state (on/off, broken, etc.) and how it appears in the lemur’s world</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.7.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">     - The problem and the moral</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.8.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">...</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.9.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">   Let’s do:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.10.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.11.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">        Group1: [ch1, ch2, ch3, ch4, ch5] -&gt; for setting, name, trait</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.12.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">        Group2: [ch6, ch7, ch8, ch9, ch10] -&gt; for light bulb origin and state</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.13.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">        Group3: [ch11, ch12, ch13, ch14, ch15] -&gt; for problem</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.14.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">        Group4: [ch16, ch17, ch18, ch19, ch20] -&gt; for resolution and moral</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.1.15.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.SS2.p4.p1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">...</span>
</span></span></span></span>
</span></span>
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">As we can see, the rough category breakdown structure is shared among the output and the reasoning trace, but the detailed structure, such as the candidate list, was different.</p>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>LLM SSoT Strategy Analysis Details</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>SSoT Strategy Analysis of Probabilistic Instruction Following</h3>

<figure id="A6.F11" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.21150v1/pif_strategy_breakdown-crop.svg" id="A6.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/531;" width="548" height="531"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>LLM strategy breakdown for biased and unbiased PIF.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We instructed gemini-2.5-flash with the prompt listed in Section <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 CoT Analysis Instruction Prompt for PIF ‣ Appendix F LLM SSoT Strategy Analysis Details ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a> to classify the LLM’s strategies when using the SSoT prompt. We fed several generated PIF outputs from deepseek-r1 to gpt-5-thinking and gpt-5-pro models to create an initial draft, and manually modified it to create classification instruction prompts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We have three axes for randomness extraction strategy: (1) Extractor, (2) Uniformizer, (3) Mapper. The “extractor” classifies how LLM converts a random string into some integer, the “uniformizer” axis classifies how LLM normalizes the generated integer for debiasing, and the “mapper” axis classifies how LLM uses the extracted integer to select an action with given probability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We used 100 responses for each action number (<math id="A6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2^{1},\dots,2^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2^{1},\dots,2^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>), both for unbiased and biased PIF, for a total <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1200=100*6*2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1200</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1200=100*6*2</annotation></semantics></math> responses. The full classification result is shown in Figure <a href="#A6.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ F.1 SSoT Strategy Analysis of Probabilistic Instruction Following ‣ Appendix F LLM SSoT Strategy Analysis Details ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">As we can see, LLM uses different strategies for the PIF task, given different configurations such as biased vs unbiased probabilities. For an unbiased PIF task, LLM tends to use a simple “linear reduce” (referred to as sum-mod strategy in the main text), “raw mod” uniformization, and then “direct mod bucket” mapping to select an action. Given a biased probability for action selection, it starts to use a more sophisticated polynomial rolling hash algorithm (which leverages the randomness of the character order as well, unlike the linear reduce approach), then performs the pow2 scaling to extract a float number in <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and then hierarchical split (i.e., if-then-else type approach for action selection) or cdf-threshold (i.e., setting the threshold value for each action given a float number in <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>) to select an action.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>SSoT Strategy Analysis of NoveltyBench</h3>

<figure id="A6.F12" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.21150v1/novelty_strategy_breakdown-crop.svg" id="A6.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/565;" width="548" height="565"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>LLM strategy breakdown for NoveltyBench.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In analysing SSoT strategy for NoveltyBench, in a similar manner to PIF, we instructed gemini-2.5-flash with the prompt listed in Section <a href="#A6.SS4" title="F.4 CoT Analysis Instruction Prompt for NoveltyBench ‣ Appendix F LLM SSoT Strategy Analysis Details ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.4</span></a> and analyzed the strategy from 10 criteria. We used 8 generations for each question in the Curated dataset, in total <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="800=8*100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>800</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">800=8*100</annotation></semantics></math> responses.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The results for all the questions and the “Creativity” category are shown in Figure <a href="#A6.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ F.2 SSoT Strategy Analysis of NoveltyBench ‣ Appendix F LLM SSoT Strategy Analysis Details ‣ String Seed of Thought: Prompting LLMs for Distribution-Faithful and Diverse Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>. As we noted in the main text, the most notable differences are the generation (referred to as “Assembly” in the main text) and randomness scope (“Sampling Scope” in the main text) criteria. Since NoveltyBench includes not only open-ended creative tasks but also closed-set tasks, which are similar to PIF, the Creative category shows qualitatively different behaviors. If LLM is given a closed set of options, there is no need to sample from a random string more than once. Also, for open-ended questions, LLM first needs to create a template that satisfies the given constraint and leverage the randomness from a random string to construct a final answer from the template.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>CoT Analysis Instruction Prompt for PIF</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the LLM’s strategy classification of PIF, we used the following prompt. We replaced the placeholders “request” and “response” with the corresponding request and response text, respectively.</p><span id="A6.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.1.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">You are a strict classifier. Read ONE response that explains how a seed becomes a choice.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Output JSON ONLY with this exact schema:</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.5.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">{</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.6.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">  "E": "crypto_hash|poly_rolling_hash|named_noncrypto_hash|linear_reduce|baseN_integer|bitstream_accum|prng_from_seed|analytic_mash|other_or_error",</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.7.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">  "U": "raw_mod|pow2_scale|big_integer_to_unit|decimal_scale|rejection_or_lemire|hash_to_float|none|other",</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.8.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">  "M": "cdf_thresholds|alias_method|hierarchical_split|rank_permute_then_index|direct_mod_bucket|inverse_transform|other_or_error",</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.9.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">  "flags": ["partial_seed_only","low_bits_only","decimal_scaling_bias","modulo_bias","boundary_unspecified","simulated_numbers","arithmetic_inconsistency","overflow_or_precision","nondeterministic_salt","uses_full_seed"],</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.10.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">  "evidence": ["short quotes..."],</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.11.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">  "confidence": 0.0-1.0</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.12.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">}</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.13.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.14.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">GENERAL RULES</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.15.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">- Classify by what is WRITTEN (keywords / formulas), not by what would be ideal.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.16.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">- If multiple hints appear, use the PRIORITY lists below. If still unclear, choose the closest label and lower confidence.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.17.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:376.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p17.1" class="ltx_p">- Always include 1–3 short evidence snippets (exact phrases or code fragments from the input).</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.18.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p18.1" class="ltx_p">- Do NOT explain your reasoning. Output JSON only.</span>
</span></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.19.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;"></span></span><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:397.5pt;"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.1.20.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="A6.SS3.p1.p1.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
